  "security_implications": "Alert classification fatal/non-fatal is determined by localparam IsFatal. In this chunk, IsFatal = {1'b0, 1'b1}, which assigns IsFatal[0]=1 (fatal) and IsFatal[1]=0 (non-fatal). This appears inverted relative to typical alert severity (alert[0] is aggregate of multiple error sources, alert[1] is only shadowed update errors). If the mapping is inverted, a non-fatal alert (alert[1]) could be treated as fatal, or a fatal alert (alert[0]) as non-fatal, leading to incorrect system response or denial of service. Additionally, the alert_test enable gating (q & qe) could be misconfigured to suppress or force test alerts. Any misconfiguration or inversion directly impacts system integrity and fault containment.",
